# ==============================================================================
# Multi-block structured meshing (MESH_MODE 1) — an EIGHT-BLOCK TWO-RING O-GRID
# around the same circular body the four-block O-grid uses.
#
#   ./run.sh -conf config/multiblock_tworing.dat
#
# What this case adds to the multi-block family:
#   * the block boundary in the middle of the fluid is a CURVE. Each of the four
#     seam edges declares `follows` (#151) on a hand-authored concentric circle,
#     so it lies on that polyline by arc length while carrying no boundary
#     condition and exporting no face;
#   * TWO radial equivalence classes instead of one, so the wall-normal law that
#     holds the first cell at BL_INITIAL_THICKNESS answers to the wall and the
#     one that reaches the far field answers to the far field;
#   * the outer ring STARTS at the height the inner ring finished at, stated in
#     the topology document, so the seam is not a jump in cell size.
#
# THE BUDGET IS THE SINGLE RING'S, EXACTLY — 4704 vertices, 9216 triangles, 192
# boundary edges — which is what makes the two meshes comparable. The comparison is
# in docs/design_notes/mesher.md and it goes BOTH ways. At the default 20 sweeps
# THIS file produces: a better-held wall spacing, a better cell shape, an identical
# non-orthogonality, and a WORSE worst wall-normal expansion ratio (1.596 against
# 1.397; 1.258 against 1.185 unsmoothed). Read it before preferring this topology.
# ==============================================================================

MESH_MODE 1
MESH_TOPOLOGY_FILE examples/topology/tworing_ogrid.json

# THREE geometries, and only two of them are boundaries. The body carries 'wall'
# in its sidecar and the far field 'farfield'; the middle ring carries 'seam',
# which reaches NOTHING — a following edge takes no condition, so if that label
# ever appeared in the .bnd it would arrive under its own name rather than hiding
# inside 'wall'.
GEOM_FILE examples/geometries/circle_body.dat
GEOM_FILE examples/geometries/circle_seam.dat
GEOM_FILE examples/geometries/circle_farfield.dat

# The wall spacing, under the name it already has. Only the INNER ring's radials
# take it; the outer ring's first cell is declared in the topology document,
# because the seam is not a wall.
BL_INITIAL_THICKNESS 0.001

MB_SPLIT_QUADS 1

# The FALLBACK. Both boundary geometries bind, so nothing should reach it — and
# the run says so, one row per patch, naming the segment each was read off.
BC_GEOM wall

EXPORT_VTK 1
EXPORT_STARCD 1
OUTPUT_FILENAME results/meshes/multiblock_tworing/mesh_multiblock_tworing.vtk
